From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:44:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0070: one pixel in four is shaded where the image is
 twice its window

--coarse-shading (KYTY_COARSE_SHADING=1) turns on VK_KHR_fragment_shading_rate and shades one
pixel in four (2x2) in draws whose viewport is at least twice the height of Kyty's window. The
window is the size the image is shown at, so those pixels were shaded four times for each one
shown; smaller draws stay exact. Without the option the extension is not enabled and pipelines
keep their dynamic states.

Astro Bot, Sky Garden, unified memory (Radeon 780M): scene at 1920x1080, 7.00 -> 7.55 images/s;
no visible difference in a 540p stream. With the game patched to a 960x540 scene the threshold
is not reached and nothing changes (8.61 -> 8.63).
